Title: GPIO write output level is called before it has been initialised

Body:
**Describe the set-up**
CubeMX 6.3.0
STM32CubeF4 Firmware Package V1.26.0 / 12-February-2021

**Describe the bug**
When selecting the gpio output to high the produced code set the pin high before it has been initialised.

**How To Reproduce**
Select gpio pin to push-pull, output to high, generate code or check with scope

1. The modules that you suspect to be the cause of the problem (Driver, BSP, MW ...).
CubeMX code genertion

2. The use case that generates the problem.
Selecting gpio to output high

3. How we can reproduce the problem.
With CubeMX

![gpio](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/51944940/133743437-69cb465e-d040-4205-9e37-47f352d38ed0.PNG)

Code produced:


static void MX_GPIO_Init(void)
{
  GPIO_InitTypeDef GPIO_InitStruct = {0};

  /* GPIO Ports Clock Enable */
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOE_CLK_ENABLE();
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOC_CLK_ENABLE();
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOF_CLK_ENABLE();
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOH_CLK_ENABLE();
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOA_CLK_ENABLE();
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOB_CLK_ENABLE();
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOG_CLK_ENABLE();
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOD_CLK_ENABLE();

  /*Configure GPIO pin Output Level */
  HAL_GPIO_WritePin(SPI1_CS_GPIO_Port, SPI1_CS_Pin, GPIO_PIN_SET);

  /*Configure GPIO pin Output Level */
  HAL_GPIO_WritePin(GPIOB, LD1_Pin|LD3_Pin|LD2_Pin, GPIO_PIN_RESET);

  /*Configure GPIO pins : PE3 PE7 PE8 PE9
                           PE11 PE12 PE13 PE14
                           PE15 PE0 PE1 */
  GPIO_InitStruct.Pin = GPIO_PIN_3|GPIO_PIN_7|GPIO_PIN_8|GPIO_PIN_9
                          |GPIO_PIN_11|GPIO_PIN_12|GPIO_PIN_13|GPIO_PIN_14
                          |GPIO_PIN_15|GPIO_PIN_0|GPIO_PIN_1;
  GPIO_InitStruct.Mode = GPIO_MODE_ANALOG;
  GPIO_InitStruct.Pull = GPIO_NOPULL;
  HAL_GPIO_Init(GPIOE, &GPIO_InitStruct);

  /*Configure GPIO pin : USER_Btn_Pin */
